# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# The community feed is the product's front door. index.html is the older
# static landing shell and is kept because ~10 pages still link to it
# directly, but it is no longer what visitors get at the root.
#
# 302 (not 301) is deliberate: a permanent redirect is cached hard by
# browsers and is painful to walk back if the root ever needs to change.
#
# Note: _routes.json scopes the Worker to /familyhub/* and /api/familyhub/*,
# so the root is served by the static asset handler and this file governs it.
# Pages resolves /forum -> forum.html automatically (clean URLs).

/            /forum   302
/home        /forum   302
/feed        /forum   302

# Retired in the mockup rebuild; keep old bookmarks and printed hotspot
# tickets landing somewhere correct instead of on a 404.
/chat        /forum   302
/chat.html   /forum   302

# Shareable short profile links: /u/bawaxict -> profile.html?user=bawaxict
# Pages placeholder syntax. profile.html?user=... remains the canonical form
# and works everywhere, including the Oracle origin.
/u/:name     /profile.html?user=:name   302
